NAME
       mode - screen resolution

SYNOPSIS
       mode
       mode <width>x<height>
       mode <width> <height>

DESCRIPTION
       Lists the resolutions the display adapter offers, marking the
       one in use, and switches to another. The console reflows to the
       new size the way it does after a font change, so the terminals
       keep their contents.

       This works on the Bochs adapter, which is what QEMU, Bochs and
       VirtualBox present. Real graphics chips need a driver of their
       own and have none here; on such a machine the command says so
       and the resolution stays as the bootloader set it.

       Full-screen programs read the size when they start, so restart
       anything already running after a switch.

NOTES
       Resolution cannot be changed through the firmware once the
       system is running: the BIOS video calls are unreachable in long
       mode and the UEFI graphics protocol is gone after boot. What is
       possible is what the adapter itself exposes.

SEE ALSO
       theme(1), setfont(1), framebuffer(2)
